<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 8347 0 R/Alt(Concentric circles around a star at the centre, which emits ionizing photons at a rate N-dot_UV. The star is surrounded by the ionized H II region, which contains a dashed circle, the rarefaction wave moving inwards. The H II region ends at a blue circle, the D-type ionization front. Outside it is a grey shell of shocked, compressed neutral gas, bounded by a thick black circle, the isothermal shock. Beyond the shock is the undisturbed neutral H I gas.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 22010 0 R>>
